WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:17.204
"Where do you think they took my parents?" Gliss asked tearfully.

2
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:24.628
"I don't know." Zann tried to answer patiently, even though Gliss had asked the same question about fifty times already.

3
00:00:24.629 --> 00:00:28.511
"It'll be okay." Perda put an arm around Gliss' shoulders.

4
00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:34.021
"We'll figure out how to save them. And Boz and all the others too."

5
00:00:34.022 --> 00:00:40.204
An hour had passed since Zann had zapped himself, Darb, and Zing to within a few paces of the Hollow.

6
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:43.717
Zing had whimpered as soon as he'd realized where they were.

7
00:00:43.718 --> 00:00:48.649
But Darb had coaxed the nervous dragon into following him and Zann into the Hollow.

8
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:57.836
They'd peered out as Morb appeared. He'd looked around in confusion, muttered a few angry words, and then zapped himself away again.

9
00:00:57.837 --> 00:01:04.524
Darb's plan had worked! Being in the Hollow had blocked whatever spell Morb was using to track Zann.

10
00:01:04.525 --> 00:01:09.242
A few minutes later, Perda and Gliss had arrived on foot.

11
00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:12.824
Now it was getting dark, and they were all still in the Hollow.

12
00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:18.652
The Hollow was a low, grassy spot protected by a thick tangle of thorny vines.

13
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:26.641
The only entrance lay between the gnarled trunks of two ancient mood trees, and nobody who didn't know it was there would ever notice it.

14
00:01:26.642 --> 00:01:29.988
Not even Morb—whoever he might really be.

15
00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:35.329
"We need to figure out how a Void got such strong magic," Zann said.

16
00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:41.481
"Enough to perform Flash Freezes, and whatever Tracking spell he was using to follow me."

17
00:01:41.482 --> 00:01:48.932
Gliss looked confused. "How would a Void get any magic at all?" she asked. "It's impossible, isn't it?"

18
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:54.465
"Not totally," Zann said. "I knew a Void when I lived in First City.

19
00:01:54.466 --> 00:02:01.751
His mom was a Red, and she infused a pair of gloves with a little bit of magic he could use each day.

20
00:02:01.752 --> 00:02:05.230
Just enough to conjure up lunch and stuff like that."

21
00:02:05.231 --> 00:02:08.898
Zann was surprised that Gliss didn't know about that sort of thing.

22
00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:12.653
Then again, she'd lived in Swamp Bottom all her life.

23
00:02:12.654 --> 00:02:20.126
There were only a few Voids in town, and most seemed content to rely on others for what little magic they needed to get by.

24
00:02:20.127 --> 00:02:24.478
It was different in the larger towns and cities, where people weren't as neighborly.

25
00:02:24.479 --> 00:02:28.412
"But that's not the kind of magic we're talking about," Perda said.

26
00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:33.379
"No magic-infused glove could do a Flash Freeze. The magic would be too weak.

27
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.216
You couldn't even use it to zap yourself six inches away."

28
00:02:37.217 --> 00:02:45.744
"I know." Zann was thinking hard. "The Directory said Morb worked in the research lab at the university, remember?

29
00:02:45.745 --> 00:02:49.858
Maybe he learned about some stronger kind of infusion.

30
00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:53.859
Researchers are always working on new forms of magic there."

31
00:02:53.860 --> 00:03:00.554
Perda looked skeptical. "If researchers were working on something that big, we would've heard about it," she said.

32
00:03:00.555 --> 00:03:05.022
"Every Void in Magica would be lining up to try it. Right, Darb?"

33
00:03:05.023 --> 00:03:10.199
Darb shrugged and kept petting Zing, who lay beside him looking anxious and miserable.

34
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.414
"I wonder how Morb got those trolls to work with him," Darb said.

35
00:03:14.415 --> 00:03:21.943
Perda shuddered. "Those trolls were scary! I never saw a real one before. Only pictures in books."

36
00:03:21.944 --> 00:03:24.680
Gliss wasn't paying much attention to the others.

37
00:03:24.681 --> 00:03:30.799
"I can't believe my parents are gone," she moaned. "We need to find them!"

38
00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.704
"I know," Zann said. "I'm worried about my grandfather too.

39
00:03:35.705 --> 00:03:38.276
But Morb got a good look at all of us.

40
00:03:38.277 --> 00:03:41.105
Who knows what he'd do if he saw us again?"

41
00:03:41.106 --> 00:03:45.757
"We already know what he'd do to you two." Perda glanced at Zann and Gliss.

42
00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.775
"He'd summon his trolls to carry you off."

43
00:03:48.776 --> 00:03:51.402
Darb stepped toward the entrance and looked out.

44
00:03:51.403 --> 00:03:54.718
"Maybe I should sneak back to town," he suggested.

45
00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:58.725
"I could let our families know what happened and see what I can find out."

46
00:03:58.726 --> 00:04:02.429
"No way," Zann said. "It's too risky."

47
00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:09.256
Perda nodded. "If we hide out here for a while, the grown-ups will take care of everything. Right?"

48
00:04:09.257 --> 00:04:14.276
Nobody said anything for a long moment. Zann felt sick and scared.

49
00:04:14.277 --> 00:04:18.066
He'd always longed for adventure and excitement. Now he'd found it.

50
00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:22.221
But somehow it wasn't nearly as much fun as he'd imagined it would be.

51
00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:26.813
Darb was still staring out into the night. "Look!" he said suddenly.

52
00:04:26.814 --> 00:04:29.950
"Here comes a message moth. We'd better see who it's for."

53
00:04:29.951 --> 00:04:33.479
Zann's heart thumped. "Are you sure that's a good idea?

54
00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.228
What if Morb can track us through it?"

55
00:04:36.229 --> 00:04:42.313
"I doubt it," Perda said. "Otherwise he would have found me and Gliss when you sent us that message earlier."

56
00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:49.958
"Right. It seemed like his Tracking spell worked by locating the person who was creating the magic," Darb said in his logical way.

57
00:04:49.959 --> 00:04:54.591
"It probably doesn't track the moth itself, or the person that it's going to."

58
00:04:54.592 --> 00:04:58.378
"I hope you're right." Zann stepped outside with the others.

59
00:04:58.379 --> 00:05:01.004
The moth immediately fluttered over to him.

60
00:05:01.005 --> 00:05:05.233
He gently held the creature in his hands, peering at it in the moonlight.

61
00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:09.761
"It's from Boz!" he said when he saw the name etched on one wing.

62
00:05:09.762 --> 00:05:16.671
The message on the other wing was inscribed in Boz's sloppy handwriting, not the neater letters that appeared when he wrote mentally.

63
00:05:16.672 --> 00:05:23.125
It read: Morb no good. Find my old diary and show it to palace.

64
00:05:23.126 --> 00:05:29.335
"That means he's alive!" Perda cried. "The Reds who disappeared are alive!"

65
00:05:29.336 --> 00:05:33.541
Gliss looked relieved. "We have to find them and save them!"

66
00:05:33.542 --> 00:05:36.947
Zann knew she was right. But it wasn't going to be easy.

67
00:05:36.948 --> 00:05:43.436
To find Boz's diary, they'd have to leave the safety of the Hollow and return to where Zann's house had been.

68
00:05:43.437 --> 00:05:47.336
Then they would need to figure out how to get to the palace in First City.

69
00:05:47.337 --> 00:05:53.281
And they'd have to do it all without any magic.
